)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@TUTORIAL: The SDSF Panels                      !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  SDSF starts with its menu. Each line of it names a panel; type the name
}  on the command line of the menu, or of any SDSF panel, to go there.
}
{  ST    }All the jobs on the JES2 queues: waiting, executing, ended.
{  I     }The jobs read in, waiting to execute or executing.
{  O     }The jobs that have ended, with output waiting to be printed.
{  H     }The jobs with held output: output kept for you to look at.
{  DA    }What is running now: the active address spaces.
{  LOG   }The system log, with the replies the system waits for.
{  PR    }The JES2 printers.     {  INIT  }The JES2 initiators.
}
}  From a job on ST, DA, I, O or H you get to two more panels:
{  ?     }the Job Data Set panel, the list of the job's output data sets
{  S     }the Output Data Set panel, the output itself
}
}  The End key takes you back: from a list to the menu, from the menu out
}  of SDSF.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next   PF10: back   PF7: list of parts   PF3: leave
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFTPAN2
  &ZUP = ISFTUTOR
)END
